bulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Perfect Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect to express an idea that something occurred before another action in the past. It can also show that something happened before a specific time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You form the tense  by using the past tense form \"to have\" plus the past participle of the verb.<br /><br /><br /> had + past participle of verb  <br /><br /><br />Here are some examples below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Event A</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Event B</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The lab crew had left the scene </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  by the time I arrived.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   I had saved him a spot at the table   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  before he showed up.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Event B</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Event A</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   The detective was very tired   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">   because he had been working the late shift.   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">    When they arrived   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">    we had already started the investigation.   </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you are writing a news article or giving an interview, you can include the Simple Past Passive to describe something done by someone at sometime in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In a regular sentence structure, you use Subject + verb + object.<br /><br /> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Governing bodies never properly carried out regulations regarding pollution.<br /><br /></span> In the Simple Past Passive form, you use the structure:<br /><br /> <span class=\"strong\">Object + was / were + past participle + by Subject</span><br /><br /> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Regulations regarding pollution were never properly carried out by any governing body</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The samples were taken back to the lab by the team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Tom's mother was remanded into custody by Johnson. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "murder ", "type": "name"}, {"con